<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.shitcoims.hunch</string>
  <!-- The capture surface's API: the loopback server the glass's coin explorer talks to.

       WHY IT IS A LAUNCHD JOB RATHER THAN A THING YOU START WHEN YOU WANT IT. The entire
       design premise is that the operator points at a coin and the desk records it in the
       same second. A capture surface that has to be started first is a capture surface that
       is down at exactly the moment worth capturing - the interesting coins arrive while
       nobody is thinking about infrastructure. So it stays up, KeepAlive, and its cost when
       idle is one process holding a bounded coin index.

       PORT 8790, and the two it deliberately is not: 8787 is the sentinel (which holds keys)
       and 8788/8799 are intel.py. A capture surface silently answering from the wrong daemon
       is worse than one that is down, because it looks like it is working.

       This process holds no key, has no RPC client and no broadcast path. Its only write is
       an append to state/hunches.jsonl. --warm builds the coin index at boot so the first
       card list the operator sees is instant rather than a cold read of the boards tail. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/uv</string>
    <string>run</string>
    <string>python</string>
    <string>-m</string>
    <string>shitcoims_paperdesk</string>
    <string>glass</string>
    <string>--warm</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/dev/joshibot</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>PYTHONUNBUFFERED</key>
    <string>1</string>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>30</integer>
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/dev/joshibot/state/logs/hunch-api.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/dev/joshibot/state/logs/hunch-api.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
